* feat(synthetic): Markdown report + client-host metadata (part 6a of #200)

Part 6 (reporting polish + version baselines, #206) lands as two PRs; this =
is the
reporting-polish half.

- Report::to_markdown(): a PR-pasteable Markdown report (metadata table + p=
er-op
  latency-vs-throughput tables) written to &lt;out&gt;.md alongside the JSO=
N. The
  console and markdown renderers share one row model (CacheView / LevelRow =
/
  op_mode_tables) so they can't drift; existing console output is unchanged=
.
- Meta.host (HostInfo via sysinfo): the client machine that ran the probe =
=E2=80=94 OS,
  kernel, CPU, physical+logical cores, memory, arch =E2=80=94 best-effort o=
ptional
  fields, #[serde(default)] for back-compat. The hostname is recorded in
  JSON/console but omitted from the pasteable markdown.
- Markdown surfaces cached_unknown (a 0% miss% can just mean &quot;no cache=
 stat&quot;).

(git SHA metadata is intentionally deferred.)

Tests: markdown content + console/markdown agreement, host summary (hostnam=
e
gating, cpu/core fallbacks), markdown_path, and old-report back-compat. Doc=
s:
readme reporting section.

Co-authored-by: Copilot &lt;223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com&gt;

* fix(synthetic): escape `|`/newlines in Markdown report table cells

Address Copilot review on #218: the Markdown metadata table interpolated
user-provided values (endpoint, graph, server image, =E2=80=A6) raw, so a v=
alue
containing `|` or a newline would break the GFM table layout. Add an `md_ce=
ll`
escaper (`|` =E2=86=92 `\|`, newline =E2=86=92 `&lt;br&gt;`, drop `\r`) and=
 apply it to every
externally-influenced table cell.

Co-authored-by: Copilot &lt;223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com&gt;

* ci(coderabbit): disable the commit-status check so rate limits can't fail=
 PR checks

Same fix as FalkorDB/JFalkorDB#339: a transient &quot;Review rate limited&q=
uot; status
shows red before CodeRabbit reads .coderabbit.yaml, and `fail_commit_status=
`
doesn't govern it, so disable the commit-status mirror entirely with
`reviews.commit_status: false`. CodeRabbit still posts reviews/comments; it=
 just
no longer adds a pass/fail check that can go red on a rate limit. Takes eff=
ect
repo-wide once merged to master.

Co-authored-by: Copilot &lt;223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com&gt;

* docs(synthetic): correct the Markdown `~` cache-stat note

Address Copilot review on #218: the note said miss% &quot;includes&quot; sa=
mples with no
cache stat, but miss% (cached_false_rate) is computed over samples with a K=
NOWN
cache stat only =E2=80=94 cached_unknown samples are excluded from its deno=
minator. The
`~` marker only flags that some samples lacked the stat; reword the note to=
 say
so.

Co-authored-by: Copilot &lt;223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com&gt;

* docs: show the client-host line in the README sample console output

Address Copilot review on #218: to_console() now prints a `client host =E2=
=80=94 =E2=80=A6` line,
so the README's sample output was out of date. Add it so the sample matches=
 what
users actually see.

Co-authored-by: Copilot &lt;223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com&gt;

