 data-pjax=3D"true" title=3D"Add TigerGraph as a benchmark vendor

Implements TigerGraph as a new graph database vendor for the benchmark suit=
e,
mirroring the Postgres/Mongo integration pattern:

- Rust backend: Vendor::TigerGraph enum plumbing, GSQL schema + query
  templates (src/tigergraph_gsql/), REST++ client (tigergraph_client.rs),
  queries repository with algorithm-query support (unlike Postgres/Mongo,
  TigerGraph natively supports pageRank/maxFlow/MSF/harmonic centrality),
  loader (tigergraph.rs), and full main.rs/lib.rs/aggregator.rs wiring.
- UI: /tigergraph comparison page, sidebar/color/multi-engine wiring, and
  TigerGraph GSQL samples in the Query Explanations hover card.
- Docs: TigerGraph capability matrix and GSQL templates in
  QUERY_EXPLANATIONS_AND_SAMPLES.md, CLI usage and Docker snippet in
  readme.md.

Elasticsearch was researched but parked for a later phase (documented in th=
e
implementation plan) since its Graph Explore API is a paid Platinum-tier
feature unsuitable for deterministic traversal benchmarking.

