<p dir=3D"auto">Postgres is modeled as a plain relational schema (<code>use=
rs</code>, <code>friend_edges</code> tables) rather than
Apache AGE; most Cypher query families have a direct SQL translation, a han=
dful
(<code>shortest_path</code>, <code>shortest_path_with_filter</code>, <code>=
all_shortest_paths_len</code>, <code>pattern_cycle</code>) are
Postgres-only (via recursive CTEs) since MongoDB's <code>$graphLookup</code=
> can't express them, and
algorithm procedures (pageRank/maxFlow/MSF/harmonic) plus vector/fulltext s=
moke queries have no
SQL equivalent and are always excluded from the Postgres catalog. See
<a href=3D"https://github.com/FalkorDB/benchmark/blob/master/QUERY_EXPLANAT=
IONS_AND_SAMPLES.md">QUERY_EXPLANATIONS_AND_SAMPLES.md</a> for the full cap=
ability
matrix and SQL templates.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Mongo connection parameters can also be supplied via enviro=
nment variables (<code>MONGO_URI</code> for a
full connection string, or <code>MONGO_HOST</code>/<code>MONGO_PORT</code>/=
<code>MONGO_USER</code>/<code>MONGO_PASSWORD</code>/<code>MONGO_DB</code>)
when no <code>--endpoint</code> is given, defaulting to <code>127.0.0.1:270=
17</code> with database <code>benchmark</code>. A
minimal local MongoDB for testing can be started with:</p>
